/* ---------- Free-atom radii, Z = 1-96 ---------- */

// Radius where the electron density of the free ground-state atom falls to 0.001 e/bohr^3
// (angstrom): M. Rahm, R. Hoffmann & N. W. Ashcroft, "Atomic and Ionic Radii of Elements 1-96",
// Chem. Eur. J. 22 (2016) 14625, doi:10.1002/chem.201602949, with the authors' corrigendum,
// Chem. Eur. J. 23 (2017) 4017, doi:10.1002/chem.201700610 (it revises several transition
// metals, e.g. Fe 2.26 -> 2.37). Values read by script from the "atomic_radius_rahm" column (pm)
// of the mendeleev package's element database, which cites both papers:
// https://github.com/lmmentel/mendeleev/raw/master/mendeleev/elements.db and docs/source/data.rst,
// retrieved 2026-10-07. Spot-checked against Figure 2 of the authors' copy of the 2016 paper,
